[E0405] Error: cannot move `tail`, which is behind a reference
    ╭─[ err/53_match_bindings/main.wip:19:32 ]
    │
 19 │     .Cons(tail, ..) => consume(tail)
    │                                ──┬─
    │                                  ╰─── a `match` binding, which refers to part of the matched value
    │
    │ Help: to take the value apart, match it with `match move …`
    │
    │ Note: a reference can read a value but cannot take ownership of it
────╯
[E0436] Error: `tail` is used after `l`, which it refers to, was changed
    ╭─[ err/53_match_bindings/main.wip:28:19 ]
    │
 26 │         .Cons(tail, ..) => {
    │               ──┬─
    │                 ╰─── `tail` refers to `l`
 27 │             l = own List::Nil
    │             ┬
    │             ╰── `l` assigned here
 28 │             show(&tail)
    │                   ──┬─
    │                     ╰─── used here
    │
    │ Help: use `tail` before `l` changes, or take what is needed from it before then
    │
    │ Note: a binding of a pattern on a place refers to the place, so the place must not change while the binding is still used
────╯
[E0413] Error: `l` is passed as `&var` together with another reference to it
    ╭─[ err/53_match_bindings/main.wip:37:34 ]
    │
 37 │         .Cons(tail, ..) => clear(&var l, &tail)
    │                                  ───┬──  ──┬──
    │                                     ╰─────────── a `&var` reference
    │                                            │
    │                                            ╰──── a `&` reference
    │
    │ Note: while a function runs, a `&var` argument must be the only reference to its place
────╯
